The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
// Missing UFS QREF clocks for UFS MEM and UFS CARD controllers
```
Reason:
The absence of the UFS QREF clocks in the clock management implementation means that the UFS MEM and UFS CARD controllers do not have the necessary clock signals to operate correctly, which can lead to failures in their functionality.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
static struct clk_branch gcc_ufs_card_clkref_en = {
	.halt_reg = 0x8c004,
	.halt_check = BRANCH_HALT,
	.clkr = {
		.enable_reg = 0x8c004,
		.enable_mask = BIT(0),
		.hw.init = &(const struct clk_init_data) {
			.name = "gcc_ufs_card_clkref_en",
			.ops = &clk_branch2_ops,
		},
	},
};

static struct clk_branch gcc_ufs_mem_clkref_en = {
	.halt_reg = 0x8c000,
	.halt_check = BRANCH_HALT,
	.clkr = {
		.enable_reg = 0x8c000,
		.enable_mask = BIT(0),
		.hw.init = &(const struct clk_init_data) {
			.name = "gcc_ufs_mem_clkref_en",
			.ops = &clk_branch2_ops,
		},
	},
};
```
Reason:
These code statements add the missing UFS QREF clocks for both the UFS MEM and UFS CARD controllers, ensuring that they receive the necessary clock signals to function properly, thus resolving the issue.

